/-!
# The common fixed line of the eleven J₄ kernel words

Select 111 independent columns from the displacement matrices of the eleven
certified kernel basis elements, and repeat one column to obtain a square
matrix. A checked right multiplier takes these
columns to the projection `v ↦ v + v 0 • cosetBaseVector`. A vector fixed by
every basis element annihilates those columns, so it lies on the base line.
All column selections and the matrix product are checked by the Lean kernel.

The source matrices and basis words are those of `KernelCount.Tables` and
`KernelCount.Relations`, descended from the literal ATLAS `J4G1-max1W1`
program in `Cardinality.Subgroup`. The supplied calculation is independent
of the ambient group order and of the assertions in GLS3 Table 5.3i.
The untrusted witness generator is retained in `FixedSpace/source/Generate.py`.
-/

